SUMMARY:Folk Art Center to Lunch Rock
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nWe meet at t
 he Folk Art Center parking area at 9:00 a.m. This is a 5 mile hike at a pr
 etty good pace (3.0 to 3.2 mph). The first half of the hike is uphill to a
  pretty stopping place/overlook. The second half is downhill.\n\nWell beha
 ved dogs on leashes are welcome to attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park near 
 where the busses typically park\, next to the woods\, closest to the Parkw
 ay.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are designed for fitness and community
  among people who are already reasonably fit. It's not an endurance hike b
 y any means\, but it is designed so we can get our hearts beating a bit wh
 ile still being able to have a conversation and meet new people.\nWhen you
  arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce ourselves briefly. There will be a
  person who is a sweep. This person is the person who walks last and makes
  sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the parking spot at 9:10. If someone n
 eeds a nature break\, we wait fo you\, but it's not a hike where we stop a
 nd take photos or frequent breaks. We basically keep hiking until the 1/2 
 way mark\, then turn around after a short (approximately 5 minute) break. 
 Then we keep that same pace on the way back. If we get on a trail right at
  9:10\, we are normally finished around 10:50.
